# W44-27 AdjustQuantBlockAC firing-rate audit

Date: 2026-05-18
Commit: see git log @ time of TSV write
Workspace: ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-27-adjust-quant-firing
Feature: investigate-adjust-quant-block-ac (gated, default-off)

## What this TSV measures

For each F-D residual cell from the W44-1 cjxl_parity_ledger:
- Per-(strategy, channel) total invocations of AdjustQuantBlockAC
- Firing counts for each of 6 heuristics (A/B/C/D/E/F bits 0-5)
- Quant change direction (unchanged/increased/decreased)
- Orig and new quant means

Heuristics:
  A: Large-transform threshold reduction (xsize > 1 || ysize > 1)
  B: Sparse-Y zero-band adjustment (c=1, sum_of_vals*8 < xsize*ysize)
  C: High-freq corner penalty (mul[c]*sum_HF >= all_nonzeros)
  D: DCT8 flatness boost (hf_nonzeros sum < 11.0)
  E: Large-transform error correction (norm_error > threshold, DCT16+)
  F: Activity-based quant reduction (only quant-DECREASE path)

## Schema

tag                strategy_code strategy_label channel total a b c d e f \
                   q_unchanged q_inc q_dec orig_q_mean new_q_mean \
                   a_pct b_pct c_pct d_pct e_pct f_pct

## Reproducer

cargo build -p jxl-encoder-cli --release --no-default-features \
  --features 'butteraugli-loop parallel investigate-adjust-quant-block-ac'

for cell in "1420710 5" "1420710 6" "1531677 4" "1531677 5" "1531677 6"; do
  set -- $cell; img=$1; d=$2
  JXL_AQBA_DIAG_TSV=benchmarks/adjust_quant_block_ac_firing_rates_2026-05-18.tsv \
    ./target/release/cjxl-rs \
    ~/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/validation/${img}.png \
    /tmp/${img}_d${d}.jxl -d $d -e 7 --quiet
done

